<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-March 17.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-March 17.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Friday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Mayne Nickless	 357.14   7.75</p>
<p> 2   Kidston Gold	   272.92   1.31</p>
<p> 3   Mt Edon Gold	   247.25   2.25</p>
<p> 4   Perilya Mines	  202.33   0.87</p>
<p> 5   Ranger Minerals	200.96   4.20</p>
<p> 6   Westpac Prop Tr	110.00   1.76</p>
<p> 7   St.Barbara Mine	104.23   0.74</p>
<p> 8   Consol Paper	    83.82   2.85</p>
<p> 9   Devex		     80.00   0.36</p>
<p>10   Tap Oil		   65.91   1.16</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Climax Mining	    2.08   1.03</p>
<p> 2   Jardine Fm China	 4.37   0.65</p>
<p> 3   Consol Rutile	    4.64   1.04</p>
<p> 4   BTR Plc		    5.86   5.45</p>
<p> 5   OLS Asia Hldgs	   7.06   0.84</p>
<p> 6   Adel Bton Cement	 7.22   1.73</p>
<p> 7   BT Aust Eq Mgmt	  7.23   0.73</p>
<p> 8   Aust Gold Rsc	    7.23   1.32</p>
<p> 9   Premier Inv		7.33   1.30</p>
<p>10   FAI Life ltd	     7.55   0.75</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
